#!/usr/bin/env python

"""Build a large grid of FSPS stellar population synthesis templates for
FastSpecFit's Bayesian grid-based, broadband-photometry-only fitting
mode.

Each grid point is a complete, fully specified stellar population model:
a Prospector-style continuity-bin star formation history, dust
attenuation, reradiated dust emission, and (optionally significant) AGN
torus emission are all computed by FSPS itself and baked directly into
the output spectrum.

Usage
-----
::

  time python bin/build-bayesian-templates --gridnumber 001 \\
      --templatedir $FTEMPLATES_DIR/bayesian

  time python bin/build-bayesian-templates --gridnumber 002 \\
      --templatedir $FTEMPLATES_DIR/bayesian --paramsfile /path/to/my-grid.yaml

``--gridnumber`` is purely a filename/provenance label (embedded in the
output filename and the ``GRIDNUM`` header keyword); it has no other
connection to ``--paramsfile``. To guard against accidentally overwriting
a grid file with a *different* grid design under the same ``--gridnumber``
(and thus the same output filename), a sha256 hash of the resolved
grid-parameter YAML's content is stored as the ``GRIDPHSH`` header
keyword; if an output file already exists for the requested ``--imf``/
``--gridnumber`` and its ``GRIDPHSH`` disagrees with the one about to be
written, the script refuses to proceed (raises rather than silently
overwriting) unless ``--force`` is given. In short: pick a fresh
``--gridnumber`` for each distinct grid design; reuse a ``--gridnumber``
only to rebuild the *same* design (e.g. after an FSPS/library update).

Grid Design
-----------
Each grid point is a single continuity-SFH age bin (``sfh=3``, constant
SFR within the bin, following the Prospector ``adjust_continuity_agebins``
prescription -- see :func:`fastspecfit.templates.continuity_agebins`)
computed with a Charlot & Fall (2000)-style power-law dust attenuation
curve (``dust_type=0``, fixed ``dust_index`` -- the same slope as
``fastspec``/``fastphot``'s own attenuation curve,
:func:`fastspecfit.templates.Templates.klambda` -- with ``dust1`` left at
its FSPS default of 0.0, i.e. no separate birth-cloud attenuation
component, and ``dust2`` (``tau``) as a free diffuse optical depth axis),
reradiated dust emission (``add_dust_emission=True``, Draine & Li 2007
templates), and AGN torus emission (Nenkova et al. 2008 templates, via
FSPS's own ``fagn``/``agn_tau`` parameters). Nebular line and continuum
emission are also included directly in the spectrum
(``add_neb_emission=True``, ``add_neb_continuum=True``).

The grid's free axes -- which parameters vary, how many grid points each
gets, and how those points are spaced -- are no longer hard-coded here:
they are read from a YAML parameter file (bundled default:
``fastspecfit/data/bayesian-grid.yaml``; override with ``--paramsfile``),
so different grid designs (more/fewer points, a different axis
combination entirely, a different prior shape for a given axis) are a
config-file change, not a code change. See that file's header comment
for the full axis schema (``kind: fixed | linspace | logspace |
exp_quantile | zero_plus_logspace | agebins``, plus ``log``/``param``/
``param_transform``/``outname``/``label``). The YAML also carries two
fixed (non-gridded) FSPS parameters applied to every model: ``dust_index``
and ``agn_tau``.

Two age-axis and grid-design constraints are baked into the code (not
YAML-configurable, since they follow directly from the physical model
rather than being a tunable grid choice):

* The age axis (``kind: agebins``) always uses
  :func:`fastspecfit.templates.continuity_agebins`, whose first two bins
  are hard-coded to 0-30 Myr and 30-100 Myr -- this both resolves the
  youngest, most rapidly evolving populations and guarantees a bin edge
  exactly at 100 Myr for the ``sfr`` column's windowed-average
  calculation below. ``nbins`` must be >= 4.
* Any axis with an exact-zero grid point (e.g. a ``tau``/``fagn``-style
  ``exp_quantile``/``zero_plus_logspace`` axis) must have ``log: false``
  in the YAML -- ``log10(0)`` is undefined, and
  :mod:`fastspecfit.fastbayes`'s sub-grid parabola refinement requires a
  well-defined coordinate for every axis.

Output Files
------------
``<templatedir>/bayesian-templates-{imf}-{gridnumber}.fits``

``FLUX`` (Primary HDU, float32 [nwave x nmodel])
    Continuity-bin SFH spectra (stellar continuum + nebular emission +
    dust attenuation + reradiated dust emission + AGN torus emission) in
    units of erg/s/cm2/Angstrom at 10 pc per solar mass formed. ``IMF``,
    ``GRIDNUM``, and the adopted solar metallicity (``ZSUN``, against
    which the ``zzsun`` axis is defined) are plain header keywords.
    Software/library provenance (loaded module versions,
    ``$FTEMPLATES_DIR``, python-fsps version and commit hash, and the
    FSPS isochrone, spectral, and dust-emission libraries in use) is
    recorded via ``desiutil.depend`` as ``DEPNAMnn``/``DEPVERnn`` keyword
    pairs, mirroring ``bin/build-templates``.

``WAVE`` (float64 [nwave])
    Native (unmodified) FSPS vacuum wavelength array in Angstroms.

``METADATA`` (table, nmodel rows)
    Per-model grid parameters: ``age`` (Gyr, mean age of the continuity
    bin), ``dt`` (Gyr, bin width), one column per non-age axis (named by
    that axis's ``name`` in the parameter YAML, e.g. ``zzsun``, ``tau``,
    ``umin``, ``gamma``, ``qpah``, ``fagn`` for the bundled default),
    ``sfr`` (Msun/yr per Msun formed, precomputed here rather than at
    ``fastbayes`` runtime as the fraction of this bin's duration falling
    within the trailing ``SFR_AVG_WINDOW_GYR`` window -- the same
    windowed-overlap formula as ``fastspecfit.continuum``'s
    ``_get_sps_properties``, specialized to a single age-bin template
    rather than a multi-bin coefficient sum), and ``mstar`` (surviving
    stellar mass fraction per solar mass formed); plus, for
    ``fastbayes``'s cheap per-object LOGL_*/DN4000_MODEL uncertainty
    estimates (see :class:`fastspecfit.fastbayes.BayesianGrid`), the
    precomputed rest-frame ``dn4000_model`` index and one
    ``<lumkey>_permass`` column (linear, per solar mass formed) for each
    of :data:`fastspecfit.fastbayes.LUM_KEYS`.

``AXES`` (table, one row per grid axis, in grid order)
    ``name``, ``log`` (whether :mod:`fastspecfit.fastbayes` refines/
    reports this axis in log10 space), ``outname`` (FASTBAYES output
    column name), and ``label`` (QA figure LaTeX label) for every axis,
    read directly from the parameter YAML -- this is what lets
    :class:`fastspecfit.fastbayes.BayesianGrid` recover the grid's axis
    list, order, and log-ness for an arbitrary axis combination without
    re-parsing YAML at fit time.

Notes
-----
* See ``bin/build-templates`` for FSPS/python-fsps installation
  instructions.

"""
import os, sys, time, hashlib
import numpy as np
import fitsio
import fsps

from astropy.io import fits
from astropy.table import Table

from fastspecfit.photometry import Photometry
from fastspecfit.util import C_LIGHT
from fastspecfit.templates import continuity_agebins
from fastspecfit.fastbayes import LUM_KEYS, LUM_WAVES, _PC_CM, _LSUN

# Averaging window for the precomputed SFR proxy (see build_bayesian_grid),
# matching the 100 Myr convention used for the main (tabular-SFH) templates
# in fastspecfit.continuum._get_sps_properties.
SFR_AVG_WINDOW_GYR = 0.1 # [Gyr] = 100 Myr

# Adopted solar metallicity (custom C3K_R10K), against which the zzsun axis
# is defined; a physical constant, not a per-grid tunable.
ZSUN = 0.0134


def _load_grid_params(paramsfile=None):
    """Load the grid axis-definition YAML file (bundled default or an
    explicit override).

    Parameters
    ----------
    paramsfile : :class:`str` or None, optional
        Full path to a grid-parameter YAML file. Defaults to the bundled
        ``fastspecfit/data/bayesian-grid.yaml`` when ``None``.

    Returns
    -------
    params : :class:`dict`
        Parsed YAML content (``axes`` list plus fixed FSPS parameters).
    paramsfile : :class:`str`
        Resolved path actually used, for provenance.

    """
    import yaml
    from importlib import resources

    if paramsfile is None:
        paramsfile = str(resources.files('fastspecfit').joinpath('data/bayesian-grid.yaml'))
    if not os.path.isfile(paramsfile):
        errmsg = f'Grid parameter file not found: {paramsfile}'
        raise FileNotFoundError(errmsg)

    with open(paramsfile) as fh:
        params = yaml.safe_load(fh)

    return params, paramsfile


def _grid_params_hash(paramsfile):
    """Short content hash of a grid-parameter YAML file, for the
    ``GRIDPHSH`` header keyword (see :func:`main`'s ``--gridnumber``/
    ``--force`` overwrite guard)."""
    with open(paramsfile, 'rb') as fh:
        return hashlib.sha256(fh.read()).hexdigest()[:16]


def _exponential_quantile_grid(npts, theta):
    """Quantile points of an Exponential(theta) distribution.

    Uses equal-probability-mass bin centers (``p_i = (i-0.5)/npts`` for
    ``i=1..npts``), i.e. each returned point is the median of its own
    ``1/npts``-probability slice of the distribution -- point density
    then follows the distribution's pdf, concentrating resolution where
    the (assumed) prior expects most galaxies to lie.

    Parameters
    ----------
    npts : :class:`int`
        Number of quantile points.
    theta : :class:`float`
        Mean (scale) of the Exponential distribution.

    Returns
    -------
    :class:`numpy.ndarray`
        Quantile values, ascending, shape ``(npts,)``.

    """
    p = (np.arange(1, npts + 1) - 0.5) / npts
    return -theta * np.log(1. - p)


def _axis_fixed(cfg):
    """Explicit list of grid values (``kind: fixed``)."""
    return np.asarray(cfg['values'], dtype='f8')


def _axis_linspace(cfg):
    """``npts`` linearly spaced values in ``[min, max]`` (``kind: linspace``)."""
    npts = cfg['npts']
    return cfg['min'] + (cfg['max'] - cfg['min']) * np.arange(npts) / np.float64(max(npts - 1, 1))


def _axis_logspace(cfg):
    """``npts`` log-uniformly spaced values in ``[min, max]`` (``kind: logspace``)."""
    npts = cfg['npts']
    lo, hi = np.log10(cfg['min']), np.log10(cfg['max'])
    return 10.**(lo + (hi - lo) * np.arange(npts) / np.float64(max(npts - 1, 1)))


def _axis_exp_quantile(cfg):
    """Exact zero plus ``npts``-1 quantiles of an Exponential(``theta``)
    distribution (``kind: exp_quantile``); see
    :func:`_exponential_quantile_grid`. Point density follows an actual
    continuous prior shape -- peaked at zero, falling off toward high
    values -- rather than an ad hoc spacing convention."""
    return np.concatenate(([0.], _exponential_quantile_grid(cfg['npts'] - 1, cfg['theta'])))


def _axis_zero_plus_logspace(cfg):
    """Exact zero plus ``npts``-1 log-spaced values in ``[min, max]``
    (``kind: zero_plus_logspace``)."""
    return np.concatenate(([0.], np.logspace(np.log10(cfg['min']), np.log10(cfg['max']), cfg['npts'] - 1)))


_AXIS_BUILDERS = {
    'fixed': _axis_fixed,
    'linspace': _axis_linspace,
    'logspace': _axis_logspace,
    'exp_quantile': _axis_exp_quantile,
    'zero_plus_logspace': _axis_zero_plus_logspace,
}


def build_bayesian_grid(imf='chabrier', paramsfile=None):
    """Build the Bayesian continuity-SFH template grid.

    Parameters
    ----------
    imf : :class:`str`, optional
        Initial mass function passed to ``python-fsps``. One of
        ``'chabrier'`` (default), ``'salpeter'``, or ``'kroupa'``.
    paramsfile : :class:`str` or None, optional
        Grid axis-definition YAML file. Defaults to the bundled
        ``fastspecfit/data/bayesian-grid.yaml`` when ``None``.

    Returns
    -------
    meta : :class:`astropy.table.Table`
        Per-model grid parameters and derived quantities (see module
        docstring).
    wave : :class:`numpy.ndarray`
        Native FSPS vacuum wavelength array in Angstroms.
    fluxes : :class:`numpy.ndarray`
        Model spectra of shape (nmodel, nwave) in units of
        erg/s/cm2/Angstrom at 10 pc per solar mass formed.
    libraries : :class:`tuple` of :class:`str`
        FSPS isochrone, spectral, and dust-emission library names, as
        reported by ``fsps.StellarPopulation.libraries``.
    axes : :class:`list` of :class:`dict`
        Resolved axis definitions, in grid order (for the ``AXES`` FITS
        extension).
    dust_index, agn_tau : :class:`float`
        Fixed FSPS parameters used for every grid point, for header
        provenance.
    paramsfile_used : :class:`str`
        Resolved grid-parameter YAML path actually used.

    """
    # https://dfm.io/python-fsps/current/stellarpop_api/
    imfdict = {'salpeter': 0, 'chabrier': 1, 'kroupa': 2}

    params, paramsfile_used = _load_grid_params(paramsfile)
    axes = params['axes']
    dust_index = float(params['dust_index'])
    agn_tau = float(params['agn_tau'])

    age_axes = [a for a in axes if a['kind'] == 'agebins']
    if len(age_axes) != 1:
        errmsg = f"Grid parameter file {paramsfile_used} must define exactly one 'agebins' axis."
        raise ValueError(errmsg)
    age_axis = age_axes[0]
    nagebins = int(age_axis['nbins'])
    if nagebins < 4:
        errmsg = f"Age axis 'nbins' ({nagebins}) must be >= 4 (continuity_agebins requirement)."
        raise ValueError(errmsg)

    non_age_axes = [a for a in axes if a['kind'] != 'agebins']
    for axis in non_age_axes:
        if axis['kind'] not in _AXIS_BUILDERS:
            errmsg = (f"Unknown axis kind '{axis['kind']}' for axis '{axis['name']}'; "
                      f'must be one of {sorted(_AXIS_BUILDERS.keys())} (or "agebins").')
            raise ValueError(errmsg)

    # Prospector-style continuity-bin lookback-time edges (Gyr); see
    # fastspecfit.templates.continuity_agebins. The first two bins are
    # hard-coded to 0-30 Myr and 30-100 Myr, guaranteeing a bin edge
    # exactly at 100 Myr for the windowed-average sfr calculation below.
    agelims = continuity_agebins(nbins=nagebins)
    agebins = np.array([agelims[:-1], agelims[1:]]).T # [nagebins, 2], Gyr
    age_mean_gyr = np.mean(agebins, axis=1) # [Gyr]
    dt_gyr = np.diff(agebins, axis=1)[:, 0]  # [Gyr]

    axis_grids = [_AXIS_BUILDERS[a['kind']](a) for a in non_age_axes]

    models_dtype = np.dtype(
        [('iagebin', np.int32)] + [(a['name'], np.float64) for a in non_age_axes])

    dims = (nagebins,) + tuple(len(g) for g in axis_grids)
    models = np.zeros(dims, dtype=models_dtype)

    for multi_index in np.ndindex(dims):
        model = models[multi_index]
        model['iagebin'] = multi_index[0]
        for iaxis, axis in enumerate(non_age_axes):
            model[axis['name']] = axis_grids[iaxis][multi_index[iaxis + 1]]

    models = models.flatten()
    nsed = len(models)

    meta = Table()
    meta['age'] = age_mean_gyr[models['iagebin']] # [Gyr]
    meta['dt'] = dt_gyr[models['iagebin']]        # [Gyr]
    for axis in non_age_axes:
        meta[axis['name']] = models[axis['name']]
    meta['mstar'] = np.zeros(nsed, 'f4')
    meta['dn4000_model'] = np.zeros(nsed, 'f4')
    for lumkey in LUM_KEYS:
        meta[f'{lumkey.lower()}_permass'] = np.zeros(nsed, 'f4')

    # Precompute the trailing-SFR_AVG_WINDOW_GYR-averaged SFR proxy per
    # template (Msun/yr per Msun formed), mirroring the windowed-overlap
    # formula in fastspecfit.continuum._get_sps_properties -- specialized
    # to a single age-bin template (coeff=1) rather than a multi-bin
    # coefficient sum: the fraction of this bin's duration overlapping the
    # trailing window, divided by the window itself (not the bin's own
    # width). Because a bin edge always falls exactly at
    # SFR_AVG_WINDOW_GYR (see above), this fraction is exactly 0 or 1 for
    # every template -- no partial-overlap case actually arises -- so
    # every sub-100-Myr bin (however many there are) reports the same
    # current-SFR value, and every older bin reports exactly zero.
    t_near = meta['age'] - meta['dt'] / 2. # [Gyr]
    t_far = meta['age'] + meta['dt'] / 2.  # [Gyr]
    frac = np.clip((np.minimum(t_far, SFR_AVG_WINDOW_GYR) - t_near) / meta['dt'], 0., 1.)
    meta['sfr'] = frac / (SFR_AVG_WINDOW_GYR * 1e9) # [Msun/yr per Msun formed]

    print('Instantiating the StellarPopulation object...', end='')
    t0 = time.time()
    sp = fsps.StellarPopulation(
        compute_vega_mags=False,
        zcontinuous=1,
        add_dust_emission=True,
        add_neb_emission=True,
        add_neb_continuum=True,
        imf_type=imfdict[imf],
        dust_type=0,            # power-law (Charlot & Fall 2000-style)
        dust_index=dust_index,  # fixed slope, matching fastspec/fastphot
        sfh=3,                  # tabular SFH (continuity bins)
    )
    print('...took {:.3f} sec'.format((time.time() - t0)))
    libraries = tuple(lib.decode() for lib in sp.libraries)
    print('FSPS libraries: {}'.format(', '.join(libraries)))

    print(f'Creating {nsed} model spectra...')
    t0 = time.time()

    lodot = 3.828e33               # [erg/s]
    tenpc2 = (10. * 3.085678e18)**2 # [cm2]

    # For the rest-frame Dn(4000)/monochromatic-luminosity precomputation
    # below, matching fastspecfit.fastbayes's own runtime formula exactly.
    fourpi_10pc2 = 4. * np.pi * (10. * _PC_CM)**2 # [cm2]

    # log progress roughly every 5% of the grid (at least every model, at most every 500)
    logevery = int(np.clip(nsed // 20, 1, 500))

    fluxes = None
    for imodel, model in enumerate(models):
        for axis in non_age_axes:
            if 'param' not in axis:
                continue
            val = model[axis['name']]
            transform = axis.get('param_transform', 'linear')
            if transform == 'log10':
                val = np.log10(val)
            elif transform != 'linear':
                errmsg = f"Unknown param_transform '{transform}' for axis '{axis['name']}'."
                raise ValueError(errmsg)
            sp.params[axis['param']] = val
        sp.params['agn_tau'] = agn_tau

        agebin = agebins[model['iagebin']] # [Gyr]
        fspstime = agebin - agebin[0]      # [Gyr], relative to bin start
        tage = agebin[1]                   # [Gyr], time of observation (bin end)

        dt_yr = np.diff(agebin)[0] * 1e9   # [yr]
        sfh_rate = np.zeros_like(fspstime) + 1. / dt_yr # [Msun/yr]

        # force the SFR to go to zero just after the bin ends
        fspstime = np.hstack((fspstime, fspstime[-1] * 1.01))
        sfh_rate = np.hstack((sfh_rate, 0.))

        sp.set_tabular_sfh(fspstime, sfh_rate)

        wave, flux = sp.get_spectrum(tage=tage, peraa=True)

        flux = flux * lodot / (4. * np.pi * tenpc2) # [erg/s/cm2/A/Msun at 10pc]

        if fluxes is None:
            npix = len(wave)
            fluxes = np.zeros((nsed, npix), dtype=np.float32)

        fluxes[imodel, :] = flux
        meta['mstar'][imodel] = sp.stellar_mass

        if sp.stellar_mass < 0:
            raise ValueError('Stellar mass is negative!')

        # Rest-frame Dn(4000) and monochromatic luminosities per solar mass
        # formed, precomputed once here (rather than once per DESI object at
        # fastbayes runtime) since both depend only on this template's
        # intrinsic rest-frame spectral shape, not on redshift or observed
        # photometry -- see fastspecfit.fastbayes.fastbayes_one for the
        # equivalent per-object formula this mirrors.
        meta['dn4000_model'][imodel] = Photometry.get_dn4000(wave, flux, rest=True)[0]
        for cwave, lumkey in zip(LUM_WAVES, LUM_KEYS):
            cflux = np.interp(cwave, wave, flux) * fourpi_10pc2 # [erg/s/A]
            if 'LOGL_' in lumkey:
                val = cflux * cwave / _LSUN / 1e10 # [1e10 Lsun]
            else:
                val = cflux * cwave**2 / (C_LIGHT * 1e13) / 1e28 # [1e-28 erg/s/Hz]
            meta[f'{lumkey.lower()}_permass'][imodel] = val

        ndone = imodel + 1
        if ndone % logevery == 0 or ndone == nsed:
            rate = ndone / (time.time() - t0) # [models/sec]
            remaining = (nsed - ndone) / rate / 60. # [min]
            print('  {}/{} models ({:.1f}%) done in {:.1f} min; ~{:.1f} min remaining'.format(
                ndone, nsed, 100. * ndone / nsed, (time.time() - t0) / 60., remaining))

    print('Finished {} models in {:.3f} min'.format(nsed, (time.time() - t0) / 60.))

    return meta, wave, fluxes, libraries, axes, dust_index, agn_tau, paramsfile_used


def main(imf='chabrier', gridnumber=None, templatedir=None, paramsfile=None, cmdline=None,
        force=False):
    """Build the Bayesian template grid and write the output FITS file.

    Parameters
    ----------
    imf : :class:`str`, optional
        Initial mass function. One of ``'chabrier'`` (default),
        ``'salpeter'``, or ``'kroupa'``.
    gridnumber : :class:`str`
        Grid identifier (e.g., ``'001'``), embedded in the output
        filename in place of a version string. Purely a filename/
        provenance label -- not otherwise linked to ``paramsfile`` -- so
        an existing output file for this ``imf``/``gridnumber`` is checked
        against the resolved ``paramsfile``'s content hash before being
        overwritten (see ``force``).
    templatedir : :class:`str`
        Root output directory; the FITS file is written directly to
        ``<templatedir>/`` (flat -- no per-grid subdirectory, since the
        filename already disambiguates by ``imf`` and ``gridnumber``).
    paramsfile : :class:`str` or None, optional
        Grid axis-definition YAML file; see :func:`build_bayesian_grid`.
    cmdline : :class:`str` or None, optional
        Exact command-line invocation, recorded verbatim as the ``CMDLINE``
        header keyword (in addition to the individual dependency/parameter
        cards already written) for easier provenance at a glance. Left out
        of the header entirely when ``None`` (e.g. calling :func:`main`
        directly, not via the command line).
    force : :class:`bool`, optional
        If ``True``, overwrite an existing output file for this ``imf``/
        ``gridnumber`` even if it was built from a different grid-parameter
        file (different ``GRIDPHSH``). Default is ``False``.

    Raises
    ------
    ValueError
        If an output file already exists for this ``imf``/``gridnumber``
        and was built from a grid-parameter file with different content
        (different ``GRIDPHSH``), and ``force`` is ``False``.

    """
    from desiutil.depend import add_dependencies, possible_dependencies, setdep

    if not os.path.isdir(templatedir):
        os.makedirs(templatedir, exist_ok=True)
    outfile = os.path.join(templatedir, f'bayesian-templates-{imf}-{gridnumber}.fits')

    # Resolve the grid-parameter file and its content hash up front (cheap --
    # just a YAML parse), so a --gridnumber/--paramsfile mismatch against an
    # existing output file is caught before paying for the (potentially very
    # slow) FSPS spectrum synthesis in build_bayesian_grid below.
    _, paramsfile_used = _load_grid_params(paramsfile)
    grid_hash = _grid_params_hash(paramsfile_used)

    if not force and os.path.isfile(outfile):
        old_hash = None
        try:
            old_hash = fitsio.FITS(outfile)[0].read_header().get('GRIDPHSH')
        except Exception:
            pass
        if old_hash is not None and old_hash != grid_hash:
            errmsg = (f"{outfile} already exists and was built from a different grid-parameter "
                      f"file (existing GRIDPHSH '{old_hash}' != '{grid_hash}' for "
                      f"'{paramsfile_used}'); refusing to overwrite a different grid design "
                      "under the same --gridnumber/--imf. Pass --force to overwrite anyway, or "
                      "use a different --gridnumber.")
            raise ValueError(errmsg)

    meta, wave, fluxes, libraries, axes, dust_index, agn_tau, paramsfile_used = \
        build_bayesian_grid(imf=imf, paramsfile=paramsfile_used)

    hduflux = fits.PrimaryHDU(fluxes)
    hduflux.header['EXTNAME'] = 'FLUX'
    hduflux.header['BUNIT'] = 'erg/(s cm2 Angstrom)'
    hduflux.header['IMF'] = imf
    hduflux.header['GRIDNUM'] = gridnumber
    add_dependencies(hduflux.header, module_names=possible_dependencies+['fastspecfit'],
                     envvar_names=('FTEMPLATES_DIR',))
    # python-fsps isn't in possible_dependencies (so add_dependencies never
    # auto-detects it), and the FSPS libraries in use aren't module versions
    # at all but configuration choices baked into this specific grid file --
    # both recorded explicitly here as dependency entries, mirroring
    # bin/build-templates.
    setdep(hduflux.header, 'PYFSPSV', fsps.__version__)
    setdep(hduflux.header, 'FSPSHASH', fsps.fsps_version.commit_id)
    setdep(hduflux.header, 'ISOCHRON', libraries[0])
    setdep(hduflux.header, 'SPECLIB', libraries[1])
    setdep(hduflux.header, 'DUSTLIB', libraries[2])
    setdep(hduflux.header, 'GRIDPARF', os.path.abspath(paramsfile_used))
    hduflux.header['GRIDPHSH'] = (grid_hash, 'sha256[:16] of the grid-parameter YAML content')
    hduflux.header['ZSUN'] = (ZSUN, 'adopted solar metallicity (custom C3K_R10K)')
    hduflux.header['AGNTAU'] = (agn_tau, 'fixed AGN torus optical depth (agn_tau)')
    hduflux.header['DUSTIDX'] = (dust_index, 'fixed power-law attenuation slope (dust_index)')
    if cmdline is not None:
        # No comment: CMDLINE's value is an arbitrary-length full invocation
        # string, and pairing it with a comment can silently truncate the
        # comment once combined they exceed an 80-char FITS card (regardless
        # of which FITS writer is used) -- the keyword name is self-
        # explanatory on its own. Written last so it doesn't visually
        # interrupt the compact bookkeeping cards above it.
        hduflux.header['CMDLINE'] = cmdline

    hduwave = fits.ImageHDU(wave)
    hduwave.header['EXTNAME'] = 'WAVE'
    hduwave.header['BUNIT'] = 'Angstrom'
    hduwave.header['AIRORVAC'] = ('vac', 'vacuum wavelengths')

    hdutable = fits.convenience.table_to_hdu(meta)
    hdutable.header['EXTNAME'] = 'METADATA'
    hdutable.header['IMF'] = imf

    axes_table = Table()
    axes_table['name'] = [a['name'] for a in axes]
    axes_table['log'] = np.array([bool(a['log']) for a in axes])
    axes_table['outname'] = [a['outname'] for a in axes]
    axes_table['label'] = [a['label'] for a in axes]
    hduaxes = fits.convenience.table_to_hdu(axes_table)
    hduaxes.header['EXTNAME'] = 'AXES'

    hx = fits.HDUList([hduflux, hduwave, hdutable, hduaxes])

    print(f'Writing {len(meta)} model spectra to {outfile}')
    hx.writeto(outfile, overwrite=True)


if __name__ == '__main__':

    import argparse

    parser = argparse.ArgumentParser(formatter_class=argparse.ArgumentDefaultsHelpFormatter)
    parser.add_argument('--templatedir', default=None,
                        help='Output directory (default $FTEMPLATES_DIR/bayesian)')
    parser.add_argument('--gridnumber', required=True, help='Grid number/identifier (e.g., 001)')
    parser.add_argument('--imf', type=str, default='chabrier', choices=['chabrier', 'salpeter', 'kroupa'],
                        help='Initial mass function')
    parser.add_argument('--paramsfile', type=str, default=None,
                        help='Grid axis-definition YAML file (default: the bundled '
                        'fastspecfit/data/bayesian-grid.yaml)')
    parser.add_argument('--force', action='store_true', help='Overwrite an existing output '
                        'file for this --imf/--gridnumber even if it was built from a '
                        'different --paramsfile (different GRIDPHSH).')
    args = parser.parse_args()

    templatedir = args.templatedir
    if templatedir is None:
        templatedir = os.path.join(os.environ['FTEMPLATES_DIR'], 'bayesian')
    templatedir = os.path.expandvars(templatedir)

    cmdline = ' '.join([os.path.basename(sys.argv[0])] + sys.argv[1:])

    main(imf=args.imf, gridnumber=args.gridnumber, templatedir=templatedir,
        paramsfile=args.paramsfile, cmdline=cmdline, force=args.force)
